==English==
[[File:Pick thickness.jpg|thumb|Measuring the '''thickness''' of a guitar [[pick]] with [[calipers]]. The measured thickness is 2.0 mm.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|thiknesse}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þicnes|t=thickness, viscosity, density, hardness; obscurity, cloud, darkness; thicket; depth, a thick body, anything thick or heavy}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|thick|ness}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|es}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The property of being [[thick]] (in dimension).
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A measure of how thick (in dimension) something is.
#: ''The '''thickness''' of the Earth's crust is varies from two to 70 kilometres.''
# {{lb|en|countable}} A layer.
#: ''We upholstered the seat with three '''thicknesses''' of cloth to make it more comfortable to sit on.''
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being thick (in consistency).
#: ''Whip the cream until it reaches a good '''thickness'''.''
# {{lb|en|uncountable|informal}} The property of being thick (slow to understand).

